  "final_answer_preview": "According to Section 80(2) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, whoever commits dowry death shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which shall not be less than seven years but which may extend to imprisonment for life. Additionally, Section 80(1) defines dowry death as the death of a woman caused by burns or bodily injury within seven years of marriage, under circumstances that indicate cruelty or harassment related to dowry demands.",
